cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use QTLSim.jl, please cite the paper whose model it implements
  (preferred-citation) and this software.
title: "QTLSim.jl: a Julia port and categorical reformulation of QTSim"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
# date-released: set when the release is made
# doi: none yet; no software DOI has been minted
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ecorecipes/QTLSim.jl"
url: "https://ecorecipes.github.io/QTLSim.jl/"
authors:
  - family-names: Frost
    given-names: Simon
abstract: >-
  A Julia port of QTSim, the quantitative-genetic simulation of Pagel, Gardner
  and Meade (Scientific Reports, 2025), validated against it bit for bit and in
  distribution, with a categorical description of its life cycle (a package
  extension on Catlab) that lowers to the Julia kernel, to SLiM/Eidos and to
  moment equations, and with density regulation, fecundity selection,
  fluctuating optima, metapopulations and several traits.
keywords:
  - quantitative genetics
  - simulation
  - moving optimum
  - stabilising selection
  - category theory
  - SLiM
  - Julia
references:
  - type: software
    title: "QTSim (QTLSim 1.0)"
    notes: >-
      The reference C implementation that QTLSim.jl ports, bundled unmodified in
      reference/QTSim. Distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.
    authors:
      - family-names: Meade
        given-names: Andrew
        affiliation: University of Reading
    year: 2023
    license: GPL-3.0-or-later
    url: "http://www.evolution.reading.ac.uk/QuantitativeGenetic/Repository.zip"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Quantitative-genetic analysis of directional adaptation suggests low maximum
    sustainable rates of change in agreement with data from field populations
  authors:
    - family-names: Pagel
      given-names: Mark
    - family-names: Gardner
      given-names: Jacob D.
    - family-names: Meade
      given-names: Andrew
  journal: Scientific Reports
  volume: 15
  year: 2025
  doi: 10.1038/s41598-025-24445-2
